<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clofesho</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th–9th centuries</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clofesho was the meeting place of a series of church councils of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> kingdoms in the 8th and early 9th centuries, held under Mercian kings and the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a>. The councils issued canons on church discipline and settled disputes over monastic lands. Its location is unknown; suggestions include Brixworth and sites near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p></div>
